{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528796-how-much-planning","id":1528796,"title":"How much planning?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-18T06:58:36-08:00","id":1528796,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How much planning?","content":"How long does it take to typically plan an attack?<br /> <br /> Suppose a pack thinks about breaking into a high-security Pentex facility, how much time is used to plan and/or prepare the attack? I think the setup and attack can frame an entire story on their own, but I want to know how other people approach it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T08:28:32-08:00","id":1528801,"title":"","content":"It's a meta answer, but planning stages should imo last no longer than they are fun. Depends on the scenario and the players, and hitting the sweet spot is sometimes difficult. Maybe just going Leeroy Jankins is the fun thing to do and as ST I can let that slide even if I've invested time in prep for security and fail-saves on the attacked side. I also had one case where players spent two sessions and the week between those planning an assault on a fortress type scenario instead. The best sign to make a cut to the next scene for me is when a player starts zoning out or the tone gets cranky between players instead of characters.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, a pack of Get will probably rely more on tactics while a pack of Shadowlords will invest more time into strategy, but overall Werewolf planning sessions tend to be a lot shorter than, say, Vampire. In my experience anyways. Werewolves are built for frontal assaults and can afford to plan with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T08:55:57-08:00","id":1528803,"title":"","content":"Forgot to mention, the <a href=\"https://bladesinthedark.com/planning-engagement\" target=\"_blank\">Blades in the Dark</a> system introduced me to Flashbacks, a mechanic that allows players to make retroactive rolls for actions they missed during the planning stage. I adapted the idea into pretty much any system I play these days (maybe a little softer) and it makes the actual assault session run much smoother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T12:42:30-08:00","id":1528824,"title":"","content":"Without something like Blades in the Dark (or hell even CofD 2e's crafting system including the idea of &quot;crafting&quot; plans), it turns into very much a group taste thing because the game itself doesn't structure the activity.<br /> <br /> Two things I think worth keeping in mind:<br /> <br /> 1) The players, and their characters have no idea what the &quot;right&quot;amount of planning is. While planning and preparation can be fun, engaging, and even be as noted worthy of being stories in their own right, they lack narrative structure. There's no obvious point of &quot;OK we're as ready as we're ever going to be,&quot; or &quot;we've prepared the right amount of special items and contingencies.&quot; You could always plan a little more, or try to think of something else to stack in your favor. A lot of bad experiences players have with planning for things comes from some players wanting to just move on, other players wanting to plan more, and the ST not balancing both desires well.<br /> <br /> While you don't have to go full Clocks since BitD already came up, a good move as a ST is to give the PCs a &quot;time budget.&quot; Like, &quot;you have four scenes to do planning and preparations before you'll miss the chance to attack the compound.&quot; First, this is vital structure (and stake setting) to give everyone expectations about how to use their in-game time. Second, it gives you tools to step in. &quot;It's obvious your characters have exhausted talking about plans for the time being, so we're going to call this the end of a scene, and if you want to have talking-planning again, it'll be another scene.&quot; Doesn't stop the players from doing more planning, but it helps make sure things are moving a long, and any less interested players don't feel like they're stuck forever waiting.<br /> <br /> 2) Plans need to matter. The second biggest thing that leads players to hate planning is that a lot of people running games take the adage of, &quot;No plan survives first contact with the enemy,&quot; as a reason to make all that planning worthless. While it's not a bad desire to want to work with the plans the PCs are making as a potential source of tension, the enemies always having the right tool to exploit a gap in the plans, NPC allies always messing up something vital, etc. only makes all the time spent on planning feel like a trap. Why play a tactician if all you're doing is feeding ideas for how you're going to fail instead of getting some real benefit out of the process?<br /> <br /> It's a tough balance (though, remember, dice exist for a reason in these things), because you don't want to make planning too powerful (though that time budget is a good way to give players a sense of how much or how little planning they really got to do and thus how off the rails things can easily get). Plans need to make the follow up not just easier to deal with, but also more fun. If one player isn't big on planning, what goes right and what goes wrong with a plan can easily be a way to keep them engaged with the end results if the plan gets them the kind of play they want to focus on (either good plans working, or flawed plans messing up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T17:10:15-08:00","id":1528850,"title":"","content":"I find it incredibly frustrating that players are incredibly keen on self-sabotaging themselves and believing no plan is up to snuff. They keep tearing apart their own ideas instead of actually trying things. It's amazing to see that they can make the opposition harder in their heads than I even imagined they would be behaving. I've tried doing the whole Blades trick with it, but they're not gelling with it and having a hard time to use the montages to cover for the prep they would have done anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T19:08:53-08:00","id":1528867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528796-how-much-planning#post1528796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does it take to typically plan an attack?<br /> <br /> Suppose a pack thinks about breaking into a high-security Pentex facility, how much time is used to plan and/or prepare the attack? I think the setup and attack can frame an entire story on their own, but I want to know how other people approach it.</div> </div> </div> </div>While running a player-driven story is what many players say they want, they still expect some structuring in how the story unfolds around them. More often than not, if I leave it entirely up to the troupe to come up with a plan, they will ignore pitfalls and try to approach problems from the front, inevitably walking into some trap (and often being annoyed the trap was there in the first place, no matter how many narrative hints I'd drop to point them out) or as you say, argue themselves out of wanting to take risks. To avoid this, I usually let the players have a good say in how they gather information to develop the plan, and I will wind up having written 3 possible entry points and exit points for a story as a summarization &quot;after considering many possible approaches, the pack decides that of them, three options seem the most likely to have success', then let them pick which of the three they go with. Usually, with a minimum of three options, it doesn't seem like trying to force their decisions. Any idea they don't go with (and elements written for them) can be recycled into future scenes or serve as a fallback if their original plan falls apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}